{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/statefulset.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:36:07.214627Z","id":"660b570308392c748cfd2cf904b7dd173f82b18af548256b338036b1e6d4c55c","body":{"detail":"Failure: `kubectl apply -k deploy/k8s/sqlite`, `deploy/k8s/postgres` or `deploy/k8s/postgres-dev` run as docs/kubernetes.md:89-92, 115-120 and deploy/k8s/postgres-dev/kustomization.yaml:5-9 show leaves every pod in ErrImagePull: no workflow in .github/workflows builds or pushes a clax-fleet image (grep for docker/ghcr/fleet finds none). Building it locally (`docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile -t ghcr.io/empathic/clax-fleet:latest .`) and `kind load docker-image` does not help, because an image tagged :latest with no imagePullPolicy defaults to Always (https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/containers/images/#imagepullpolicy-defaulting), so the kubelet still pulls from the registry. postgres-dev exists precisely for kind and minikube. The same image line is deploy/k8s/postgres/deployment.yaml:45. Beyond first use, a mutable :latest means a pod rescheduled for any reason can pull a newer build than its siblings, mixing versions with no rollout.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"5be5484c159e8eb07ff75e3da8843103827220a93f34e31baffd33d421367846"},"suggested_fix":"Give the base workloads an image with a fixed, non-latest tag and drive it through a kustomize `images:` entry in each overlay (so `kustomize edit set image clax-fleet=<registry>/clax-fleet:<tag>` is the one documented change), set imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent in postgres-dev, and add the kind steps (docker build, kind load docker-image, set image) to docs/kubernetes.md before the apply commands; or publish the image from release.yml.","summary":"The manifests name ghcr.io/empathic/clax-fleet:latest, which nothing publishes, and :latest makes kubelet ignore an image loaded into kind or minikube","tags":["review","review:k8s-deep","devops","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/kustomization.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:36:07.215041Z","id":"7029daac331092edcdc6aad90e21f4c652a3301c4de083be06108cb118f5a0ab","body":{"detail":"CLAX_FLEET_SHARDS (deploy/k8s/sqlite/statefulset.yaml:46-47) must equal replicas, and a pod past it refuses to start (crates/clax-fleet/src/main.rs:200-203). Changing an env var in the template is a new revision, so adding one shard rolls clax-0 … clax-N-1 one by one, each shard's instances down for its restart, although none of them change. `kubectl scale sts clax --replicas=3`, the usual command, instead leaves clax-2 crash-looping. docs/kubernetes.md:102-103 does not warn of either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":7},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"a59428e34a1b2182cbf2fc4ecd202f3eb7fc021b9fdc86b1c6dbbf454a22fc54"},"suggested_fix":"Have serve take the shard count from somewhere that does not restart pods (for example a top-level `shards = N` in the catalog, which every pod already reloads without restarting); at least document that raising CLAX_FLEET_SHARDS restarts every shard.","summary":"Scaling the SQLite fleet out means editing CLAX_FLEET_SHARDS in the pod template, which restarts every existing shard","tags":["review","review:k8s-deep","devops","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/statefulset.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:36:07.215108Z","id":"89f66f73417556971090a622883db0182230425f1dbdf6464493f28fc00009de","body":{"detail":"Unlike deploy/k8s/postgres/deployment.yaml:28-35, the StatefulSet sets no topologySpreadConstraints, so several shards, each the only home of its instances, can land on one node and fail together. With fsGroup: 10001 and no fsGroupChangePolicy, the kubelet changes ownership recursively on every mount (https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/configure-pod-container/security-context/#configure-volume-permission-and-ownership-change-policy-for-pods), which slows each shard's start as homes grow and counts against the startupProbe's 60 s.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":33},"content_hash":"3c6713c8f34d442998f784f3e6368e82ea0ba39acbba78ee60626582a77ab92a"},"suggested_fix":"Add the same topologySpreadConstraints as the Deployment, and `fsGroupChangePolicy: OnRootMismatch` to the pod securityContext.","summary":"The SQLite StatefulSet has no topology spread, and its fsGroup makes the kubelet re-own every file on each volume at every start","tags":["review","review:k8s-deep","devops","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/statefulset.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:41:04.886006Z","id":"68fda5a43fdad640ac58992a31655e407fd4dc48c69f4444c1a19309a6df4ff3","body":{"detail":"No workflow in .github/workflows (ci.yml, native-check.yml, publish-pi.yml, release.yml) mentions docker, ghcr, an image or clax-fleet, and deploy/k8s/sqlite/statefulset.yaml:36 and deploy/k8s/postgres/deployment.yaml:45 name ghcr.io/empathic/clax-fleet:latest with no imagePullPolicy. But docs/kubernetes.md:46-53 ('The image', before both deploy sections) says to build '<registry>/clax-fleet:<tag>' and, 'Before applying, point the manifests' image: at your tag (with kustomize edit set image ghcr.io/empathic/clax-fleet=<registry>/clax-fleet:<tag> in an overlay of your own)'. A user who follows that gets a non-latest tag, whose pull policy defaults to IfNotPresent (https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/containers/images/#imagepullpolicy-defaulting), so a kind-loaded image is used. The failure arises only when the image step is skipped; the gap is that deploy/k8s/postgres-dev/kustomization.yaml:5-9 and deploy/k8s/sqlite/kustomization.yaml:4-5 show the apply without it. Overlaps the existing suggestion b735b950ce14f9374b8d2171fefa303f3e8808c61bf40053595991e51f362e5a on the :latest tag.","kind":"comment","references":"660b570308392c748cfd2cf904b7dd173f82b18af548256b338036b1e6d4c55c","summary":"downgraded: concern — the :latest default image is unpublished, but the documented steps set one's own tag first","tags":["verified:downgraded","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/kustomization.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:41:21.161870Z","id":"caa5dbc6043ee5999eb6abcd0fa6ac98f7d321c536eec61ba317360ad84ef9f5","body":{"detail":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/statefulset.yaml:46-47 sets CLAX_FLEET_SHARDS in the template and :10-11 uses RollingUpdate; a template change updates each pod in turn, and podManagementPolicy: Parallel (line 9) does not apply to updates (https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/controllers/statefulset/#rolling-updates). crates/clax-fleet/src/main.rs:200-203 refuses ordinal >= shards. deploy/k8s/sqlite/kustomization.yaml:7-10 and docs/kubernetes.md:102-103 say to raise both together without mentioning the restarts.","kind":"comment","references":"7029daac331092edcdc6aad90e21f4c652a3301c4de083be06108cb118f5a0ab","summary":"confirmed: raising CLAX_FLEET_SHARDS changes the pod template and rolls every shard; kubectl scale alone crash-loops the new pod","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/statefulset.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:41:21.163554Z","id":"d28a4123e453a1433aff1f680e11bc81c64111276c11a0c350dd8ab524e73079","body":{"detail":"grep -n 'topologySpread|fsGroupChangePolicy' deploy/k8s/sqlite/statefulset.yaml finds nothing, while deploy/k8s/postgres/deployment.yaml:28-35 has topologySpreadConstraints; statefulset.yaml:27-33 sets fsGroup: 10001. Without fsGroupChangePolicy the kubelet changes ownership recursively on every mount (https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/configure-pod-container/security-context/#configure-volume-permission-and-ownership-change-policy-for-pods). One correction: that chown happens while the volume is mounted, before the container starts, so it delays the start but does not count against the startupProbe (statefulset.yaml:68-73), which runs only once the container has started.","kind":"comment","references":"89f66f73417556971090a622883db0182230425f1dbdf6464493f28fc00009de","summary":"confirmed: no topology spread on the StatefulSet, and fsGroup without fsGroupChangePolicy","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/statefulset.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:42:05.465799Z","id":"e8cbc2c2f344e4b1789ba7738af3a8fc79147f08f7f9528daea779dff9882b4f","body":{"detail":"`kubectl apply -k deploy/k8s/sqlite`, `deploy/k8s/postgres` or `deploy/k8s/postgres-dev` run as docs/kubernetes.md:89-92, 115-120 and deploy/k8s/postgres-dev/kustomization.yaml:5-9 show leaves every pod in ErrImagePull: no workflow in .github/workflows builds or pushes a clax-fleet image (grep for docker/ghcr/fleet finds none). Building it locally (`docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile -t ghcr.io/empathic/clax-fleet:latest .`) and `kind load docker-image` does not help, because an image tagged :latest with no imagePullPolicy defaults to Always (https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/containers/images/#imagepullpolicy-defaulting), so the kubelet still pulls from the registry. postgres-dev exists precisely for kind and minikube. The same image line is deploy/k8s/postgres/deployment.yaml:45. Beyond first use, a mutable :latest means a pod rescheduled for any reason can pull a newer build than its siblings, mixing versions with no rollout.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"5be5484c159e8eb07ff75e3da8843103827220a93f34e31baffd33d421367846"},"suggested_fix":"Give the base workloads an image with a fixed, non-latest tag and drive it through a kustomize `images:` entry in each overlay (so `kustomize edit set image clax-fleet=<registry>/clax-fleet:<tag>` is the one documented change), set imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent in postgres-dev, and add the kind steps (docker build, kind load docker-image, set image) to docs/kubernetes.md before the apply commands; or publish the image from release.yml.","summary":"The manifests name ghcr.io/empathic/clax-fleet:latest, which nothing publishes, and :latest makes kubelet ignore an image loaded into kind or minikube","supersedes":"660b570308392c748cfd2cf904b7dd173f82b18af548256b338036b1e6d4c55c","tags":["review","review:k8s-deep","devops","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/kustomization.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:00:22.185598Z","id":"79dc362d295cc8652754185595399ebc627cdf3b943fc3a4290eb486421910bf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:347050368","summary":"The number of shards is the catalog's `shards` (every pod reloads it); CLAX_FLEET_SHARDS is gone from the StatefulSet; a pod past the shards serves nothing and logs so; docs and sqlite/kustomization.yaml give `kubectl scale sts` after raising shards.","supersedes":"7029daac331092edcdc6aad90e21f4c652a3301c4de083be06108cb118f5a0ab","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/statefulset.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:00:22.265933Z","id":"f71f3e4a2691b6f879cf83772c6246b3b1f341693e0268cb1c8dbd36e362cc4b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:347050368","summary":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/statefulset.yaml has topologySpreadConstraints across hostnames and fsGroupChangePolicy: OnRootMismatch.","supersedes":"89f66f73417556971090a622883db0182230425f1dbdf6464493f28fc00009de","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/statefulset.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:00:22.346470Z","id":"c54a9d027ae6fabd8c30c564ebb91bffedc213d582c7c517ab42586b160fb3ed","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:347050368","summary":"The overlays name the image through kustomize `images`; .github/workflows/fleet-image.yml publishes ghcr.io/<owner>/clax-fleet for each release tag; postgres-dev sets imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent; docs/kubernetes.md gives the kind steps (build, kind load, kustomize edit set image).","supersedes":"e8cbc2c2f344e4b1789ba7738af3a8fc79147f08f7f9528daea779dff9882b4f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/kustomization.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:06:57.772627Z","id":"fe7b8911bba3c43a6fdb135c8e3e60132a644ab206c9c8c131f461ba1f82643f","body":{"detail":"Failure: following docs/kubernetes.md, Deploying on SQLite (lines 149-154) or on PostgreSQL (181-187), `kubectl apply -k deploy/k8s/sqlite` leaves every pod in ImagePullBackOff. The tag v0.6.0 (40a578ec7, 2026-10-21) is an ancestor of this branch and contains neither deploy/Dockerfile nor .github/workflows/fleet-image.yml (`git ls-tree -r --name-only v0.6.0 -- deploy .github/workflows` lists only ci.yml, native-check.yml, publish-pi.yml, release.yml), so the tag-push trigger has already passed and a workflow_dispatch at that ref finds no workflow. Likewise docs/kubernetes.md:67 points kustomize at `github.com/empathic/clax//deploy/k8s/postgres?ref=v0.6.0`, a path that does not exist at that ref, and :131 runs check-catalog from the same missing image. deploy/k8s/postgres/kustomization.yaml:20-23 has the same pin. scripts/release.sh never edits deploy/k8s or docs/kubernetes.md (`grep -n 'newTag\\|deploy/k8s' scripts/release.sh` is empty), so after each later release the manifests still name 0.6.0. Record e8cbc2c2 (closed by c54a9d02) was about :latest; the replacement tag has the same defect.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"e47d6c202815fa049477d14a2f49caba9a4f18d7a922e224c7d6e977b2d0a84e"},"suggested_fix":"Until a release that carries the workflow is tagged, have the overlays' comments and docs build the image first (the kind steps at docs/kubernetes.md:81-88) and say the published image starts at the next version. Make scripts/release.sh set newTag in both overlays and the version in docs/kubernetes.md's examples, with a check in scripts/test-release-script.sh.","summary":"Both overlays name ghcr.io/empathic/clax-fleet:0.6.0, an image no workflow can publish, and the release script never moves the tag","tags":["review","review:k8s-deep-2","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/statefulset.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:06:57.772751Z","id":"999b16cf36337d3348cdb1974cc5033786023f4fe1e08628c149c1813b44de70","body":{"detail":"statefulset.yaml:78-81 has `secretRef: name: clax-secrets, optional: true`; the PostgreSQL Deployment (deployment.yaml:83-85) requires it. With the Secret absent, serve() (crates/clax-fleet/src/main.rs:316-324) generates a different random key per shard and only warns, so no shard believes another's forwarding headers, `clax-fleet status --backend sqlite` refuses for lack of CLAX_FLEET_PEER_KEY (main.rs:494-498), and each instance's /setup stays closed (docs/kubernetes.md:144-145). The deployment looks healthy (probes pass) while it is misconfigured, and the fix later needs a rollout restart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":74},"end":{"line":81},"content_hash":"59122ee2af1b7426c0acac49589ac8e7b187da5f0542675588b88f3eb2395224"},"suggested_fix":"Drop `optional: true`, and on the SQLite backend refuse to start without CLAX_FLEET_PEER_KEY (as the PostgreSQL backend refuses without CLAX_KEK), or keep the fallback only behind an explicit flag for single-shard trials.","summary":"The SQLite StatefulSet marks clax-secrets optional, so a missing or misnamed Secret starts every shard with a random peer key of its own and no setup secrets, with only a log warning","tags":["review","review:k8s-deep-2","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/kustomization.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:14.036097Z","id":"0432de1243f26fb510b527dffc32ae4ace1f83610af047939cac25fe0b591b39","body":{"detail":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/kustomization.yaml:21-24 and deploy/k8s/postgres/kustomization.yaml (images block) both set newName ghcr.io/empathic/clax-fleet, newTag \"0.6.0\". `git merge-base --is-ancestor v0.6.0 HEAD` succeeds, and `git ls-tree -r --name-only v0.6.0 -- deploy .github/workflows` lists only .github/workflows/{ci,native-check,publish-pi,release}.yml (plus .qual): no deploy/Dockerfile, no fleet-image.yml, no deploy/k8s. docs/kubernetes.md:67 references `github.com/empathic/clax//deploy/k8s/postgres?ref=v0.6.0` and :131 runs ghcr.io/empathic/clax-fleet:0.6.0. `grep -n 'newTag\\|deploy/k8s\\|kubernetes' scripts/release.sh` is empty, so a later release leaves the pin at 0.6.0. Pulling a tag that was never pushed gives ImagePullBackOff.","kind":"comment","references":"fe7b8911bba3c43a6fdb135c8e3e60132a644ab206c9c8c131f461ba1f82643f","summary":"confirmed: both overlays pin clax-fleet:0.6.0, which no workflow at v0.6.0 could have built, and release.sh never bumps it","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/statefulset.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:14.037326Z","id":"c1141c3b5ff3950b0a5eb9bd916bbaf783532750d3e4d28c9b2f344b1bd9eebb","body":{"detail":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/statefulset.yaml:78-81 `secretRef: name: clax-secrets, optional: true`; deploy/k8s/postgres/deployment.yaml:83-85 has no optional. crates/clax-fleet/src/main.rs:316-324: with no peer_key on SQLite it logs tracing::warn! and uses random_key(), different per process. main.rs:494-498 `clax-fleet status` on SQLite errors without CLAX_FLEET_PEER_KEY. docs/kubernetes.md:140-145 says a missing setup secret only logs that /setup stays closed. Probes (/healthz, /readyz) do not depend on the Secret, so pods report healthy.","kind":"comment","references":"999b16cf36337d3348cdb1974cc5033786023f4fe1e08628c149c1813b44de70","summary":"confirmed: clax-secrets is optional on SQLite, and a missing key yields a per-shard random key with only a warning","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/kustomization.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T04:09:42.308246Z","id":"da2b1cced30584770173dcf691e9564382c76998e427d663d840273bab95da87","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e6b59f7af","summary":"scripts/bump-version.sh writes newTag in both overlays and the version in docs/kubernetes.md's examples, check-version.sh checks them, and the overlays and docs say the first published image is the release after 0.6.0 and to build it until then. Test: //scripts:release. Evidence: `just ci` at e6b59f7af passes the clax-fleet, clax-pagevfs, scripts and manifest tests (357 of 361; the 4 failures are clax-server api_seats::load_150_people_on_100_seats and //apps/clax_app:apk_test, which fail on main too, and two web e2e lanes that passed when rerun alone). PostgreSQL tests are ignored without CLAX_TEST_PG_URL.","supersedes":"fe7b8911bba3c43a6fdb135c8e3e60132a644ab206c9c8c131f461ba1f82643f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/sqlite/statefulset.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T04:09:42.390152Z","id":"4b2be473123e753d102785be545f9ede4cc8ffeebc1e4d0f3fc85431f605d432","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e6b59f7af","summary":"The SQLite backend refuses to start without CLAX_FLEET_PEER_KEY, and the StatefulSet's clax-secrets secretRef is no longer optional. Test: tests::the_sqlite_backend_needs_the_peer_key. Evidence: `just ci` at e6b59f7af passes the clax-fleet, clax-pagevfs, scripts and manifest tests (357 of 361; the 4 failures are clax-server api_seats::load_150_people_on_100_seats and //apps/clax_app:apk_test, which fail on main too, and two web e2e lanes that passed when rerun alone). PostgreSQL tests are ignored without CLAX_TEST_PG_URL.","supersedes":"999b16cf36337d3348cdb1974cc5033786023f4fe1e08628c149c1813b44de70","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
